   "message": "SEB-301: home nav repeat fix and agreed words (25 Oct) (#695)\n\n* SEB-301: home top order, clearer official-rate table, year menu from 2020, research list and page tidy\n\nHome top: headline, subhead, body, then the agents line as a quiet footnote, no bold numbers.\nOfficial-rate table: only moves with a real gap before, share of the gap closed with a bar, new words.\nYear menu: only years with 10+ priced countries (menu_years in index.json), select no longer clipped in Safari.\nResearch: list rows instead of a grey card; grid fills the column, ink links, capitalised names, no -0.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\n* SEB-301: home top styles apply to the home page only (finding and country pages also have #hero)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\n* SEB-301: home nav no longer repeats in an open tab; three agreed word changes\n\nThe home nav was appended again on every new hour (siteLive reload), so a tab left open showed the links two or three times.\nWords agreed with Seb in chat, 25 Oct: whatLine routes sentence, home findings title 'What we found', Findings page heading.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\n* SEB-301: Findings intro drops the repeat of the new heading (Seb, 25 Oct)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
