   "date": "2026-10-25T02:39:59Z",
   "email": "person",
   "message": "SEB-301: CLAUDE.md, nothing waits for a green run (automerge merges, the rendered gates are the page check) (#672)\n\nReplaces yesterday's 'poll CI in the background' line: web sessions are not allowed to poll, so they stopped.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  },
  {
   "sha": "4a7759224fe227a4c8fc51de1d3b40ab2bbee327",
   "html_url": "https://github.com/SebR214/margin/commit/4a7759224fe227a4c8fc51de1d3b40ab2bbee327",
   "date": "2026-10-25T02:34:28Z",
   "email": "person",
   "message": "SEB-301: no label from Seb on writer PRs, and sessions wait for CI instead of stopping (#670)\n\n- check_copy_lock.py already passes a PR whose title names its SEB issue (since 8 Oct). Its header still said the\n  label was required, and agents/run_writer.sh titled its PRs without an issue and told Seb to add 'copy-approved'.\n  The writer now puts the issue in the title (second argument, SEB-301 by default), and both texts say no label.\n- CLAUDE.md: a writer PR titled with its SEB issue needs no label, never ask Seb for one. New working rule: waiting is\n  not stopping. A session waits for CI, merges and short clocks itself with a background poll, then does the next\n  step; it stops only when the job is merged and checked live, or truly needs Seb.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
